{"id":"mahabharata-8-009","work":"mahabharata","part":8,"partName":"कर्णपर्व","partNameEn":"Karna Parva","unit":9,"title":"नवमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 9 · Karna's slaughter of the Pandava army","summary":{"en":"Karna cuts through the Pandava army with arrows, and the brothers Ashvatthaman and others stand against the attackers. The Kekaya and other forces are driven back with great loss.","kn":"ಕರ್ಣ ಬಾಣಗಳಿಂದ ಪಾಂಡವ ಸೈನ್ಯವನ್ನು ಸೀಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಅಶ್ವತ್ಥಾಮ ಮೊದಲಾದ ಸೋದರರು ದಾಳಿಕೋರರನ್ನು ಎದುರಿಸುತ್ತಾರೆ. ಕೇಕಯ ಮೊದಲಾದ ಪಡೆಗಳು ಭಾರೀ ನಷ್ಟದೊಂದಿಗೆ ಹಿಂದೆ ಸರಿಯುತ್ತವೆ.","hi":"कर्ण बाणों से पाण्डव सेना को चीरता है, और अश्वत्थामा आदि आक्रमणकारियों का सामना करते हैं। केकय आदि सेनाएँ भारी हानि के साथ पीछे हटा दी जाती हैं।","te":"కర్ణుడు బాణాలతో పాండవసేనను చీల్చుతాడు; అశ్వత్థామ తదితరులు దాడి చేసేవారిని ఎదుర్కొంటారు. కేకయ మొదలైన బలగాలు భారీ నష్టంతో వెనక్కి తరమబడతాయి.","ta":"கர்ணன் அம்புகளால் பாண்டவப் படையைப் பிளக்க, அஸ்வத்தாமன் முதலியோர் தாக்குபவரை எதிர்க்கின்றனர். கேகயர் முதலிய படைகள் பேரிழப்புடன் பின்னுக்குத் தள்ளப்படுகின்றன.","ml":"കർണ്ണൻ അമ്പുകൾകൊണ്ട് പാണ്ഡവസേനയെ പിളർക്കുന്നു; അശ്വത്ഥാമാവും മറ്റുള്ളവരും ആക്രമിക്കുന്നവർക്കെതിരെ നിൽക്കുന്നു. കേകയരും മറ്റു സേനകളും വലിയ നഷ്ടത്തോടെ പിന്തിരിപ്പിക്കപ്പെടുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 8.9; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Jul 29 2019","sections":[{"title":"कर्णपर्व","titleEn":"Karna Parva","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"ततः कर्णो महेष्वासः पाण्डवानामनीकिनीम् ।\nजघान समरे शूरः शरैः संनतपर्वभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the great archer Karna, the hero, slew the Pandava army in the battle with arrows with smoothly bent joints."}},{"n":2,"text":"तथैव पाण्डवा राजंस्तव पुत्रस्य वाहिनीम् ।\nकर्णस्य प्रमुखे क्रुद्धा विनिजघ्नुर्महारथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"And likewise the Pandavas, great chariot-fighters, angry, struck down your son's host at the head of Karna's force, O king."}},{"n":3,"text":"कर्णो राजन्महाबाहुर्न्यवधीत्पाण्डवीं चमूम् ।\nनाराचैरर्करश्म्याभैः कर्मारपरिमार्जितैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Karna, strong-armed, O king, slaughtered the Pandava host with iron arrows that gleamed like the sun's rays, polished by the smith."}},{"n":4,"text":"तत्र भारत कर्णेन नाराचैस्ताडिता गजाः ।\nनेदुः सेदुश्च मम्लुश्च बभ्रमुश्च दिशो दश ॥","meaning":{"en":"There, O Bharata, elephants struck by Karna's iron arrows bellowed, sank down, grew faint and wandered in all ten directions."}},{"n":5,"text":"वध्यमाने बले तस्मिन्सूतपुत्रेण मारिष ।\nनकुलोऽभ्यद्रवत्तूर्णं सूतपुत्रं महारणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"As that force was being slaughtered by the charioteer's son, my lord, Nakula quickly rushed at the charioteer's son in the great battle."}},{"n":6,"text":"भीमसेनस्तथा द्रौणिं कुर्वाणं कर्म दुष्करम् ।\nविन्दानुविन्दौ कैकेयौ सात्यकिः समवारयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhimasena met Drona's son, who was performing a hard deed; Satyaki checked the two Kekayas Vinda and Anuvinda."}},{"n":7,"text":"श्रुतकर्माणमायान्तं चित्रसेनो महीपतिः ।\nप्रतिविन्ध्यं तथा चित्रश्चित्रकेतनकार्मुकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"King Chitrasena met Shrutakarman as he came on, and Chitra, with his bow and wondrous banner, met Prativindhya."}},{"n":8,"text":"दुर्योधनस्तु राजानं धर्मपुत्रं युधिष्ठिरम् ।\nसंशप्तकगणान्क्रुद्धो अभ्यधावद्धनंजयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Duryodhana advanced on King Yudhishthira, son of Dharma; Dhananjaya, angry, rushed at the bands of Samshaptakas."}},{"n":9,"text":"धृष्टद्युम्नः कृपं चाथ तस्मिन्वीरवरक्षये ।\nशिखण्डी कृतवर्माणं समासादयदच्युतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In that destruction of the best of heroes, Dhrishtadyumna engaged Kripa, and Shikhandin the unfailing Kritavarman."}},{"n":10,"text":"श्रुतकीर्तिस्तथा शल्यं माद्रीपुत्रः सुतं तव ।\nदुःशासनं महाराज सहदेवः प्रतापवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shrutakirti engaged Shalya, and Madri's son the valiant Sahadeva engaged your son Duhshasana, great king."}},{"n":11,"text":"केकयौ सात्यकिं युद्धे शरवर्षेण भास्वता ।\nसात्यकिः केकयौ चैव छादयामास भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the battle the two Kekayas covered Satyaki with a blazing rain of arrows, and Satyaki covered the two Kekayas, O Bharata."}},{"n":12,"text":"तावेनं भ्रातरौ वीरं जघ्नतुर्हृदये भृशम् ।\nविषाणाभ्यां यथा नागौ प्रतिनागं महाहवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"The two brothers struck that hero hard in the chest, as two elephants strike a rival elephant with their tusks in a great fight."}},{"n":13,"text":"शरसंभिन्नवर्माणौ तावुभौ भ्रातरौ रणे ।\nसात्यकिं सत्यकर्माणं राजन्विव्यधतुः शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Their armour pierced by arrows, the two brothers in the battle wounded Satyaki, true in deed, with arrows, O king."}},{"n":14,"text":"तौ सात्यकिर्महाराज प्रहसन्सर्वतोदिशम् ।\nछादयञ्शरवर्षेण वारयामास भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Satyaki, laughing, covering them on all sides with a rain of arrows, held them back, O Bharata."}},{"n":15,"text":"वार्यमाणौ ततस्तौ तु शैनेयशरवृष्टिभिः ।\nशैनेयस्य रथं तूर्णं छादयामासतुः शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Held back by the showers of Shini's grandson's arrows, they quickly covered his chariot with arrows."}},{"n":16,"text":"तयोस्तु धनुषी चित्रे छित्त्वा शौरिर्महाहवे ।\nअथ तौ सायकैस्तीक्ष्णैश्छादयामास दुःसहैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The son of Shini, cutting their wondrous bows in the great fight, then covered them with sharp and unbearable arrows."}},{"n":17,"text":"अथान्ये धनुषी मृष्टे प्रगृह्य च महाशरान् ।\nसात्यकिं पूरयन्तौ तौ चेरतुर्लघु सुष्ठु च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the two, taking other polished bows and great arrows, moved swiftly and skilfully, filling Satyaki with arrows."}},{"n":18,"text":"ताभ्यां मुक्ता महाबाणाः कङ्कबर्हिणवाससः ।\nद्योतयन्तो दिशः सर्वाः संपेतुः स्वर्णभूषणाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Great arrows loosed by them, with feathers of heron and peacock, adorned with gold, fell lighting up all directions."}},{"n":19,"text":"बाणान्धकारमभवत्तयो राजन्महाहवे ।\nअन्योन्यस्य धनुश्चैव चिच्छिदुस्ते महारथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A darkness of arrows arose between them in the great battle, O king, and those great chariot-fighters cut each other's bows."}},{"n":20,"text":"ततः क्रुद्धो महाराज सात्वतो युद्धदुर्मदः ।\nधनुरन्यत्समादाय सज्यं कृत्वा च संयुगे ।\nक्षुरप्रेण सुतीक्ष्णेन अनुविन्दशिरोऽहरत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, enraged, the Satvata, wild in battle, took another bow, strung it in the battle, and with a very sharp razor-edged arrow cut off Anuvinda's head."}},{"n":21,"text":"तच्छिरो न्यपतद्भूमौ कुण्डलोत्पीडितं महत् ।\nशम्बरस्य शिरो यद्वन्निहतस्य महारणे ।\nशोषयन्केकयान्सर्वाञ्जगामाशु वसुंधराम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That head, with its earrings pressed, fell to the ground, like the head of Shambara killed in the great battle, drying up all the Kekayas."}},{"n":22,"text":"तं दृष्ट्वा निहतं शूरं भ्राता तस्य महारथः ।\nसज्यमन्यद्धनुः कृत्वा शैनेयं प्रत्यवारयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing that hero killed, his great chariot-fighter brother took another strung bow and held back Shini's grandson."}},{"n":23,"text":"स शक्त्या सात्यकिं विद्ध्वा स्वर्णपुङ्खैः शिलाशितैः ।\nननाद बलवन्नादं तिष्ठ तिष्ठेति चाब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Piercing Satyaki with a spear and with gold-feathered arrows whetted on stone, he roared loudly and cried, \"Stand! Stand!\""}},{"n":24,"text":"स सात्यकिं पुनः क्रुद्धः केकयानां महारथः ।\nशरैरग्निशिखाकारैर्बाह्वोरुरसि चार्दयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Again angry, that great chariot-fighter of the Kekayas pained Satyaki in the arms and chest with arrows shaped like flames of fire."}},{"n":25,"text":"स शरैः क्षतसर्वाङ्गः सात्वतः सत्त्वकोविदः ।\nरराज समरे राजन्सपत्र इव किंशुकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With all his limbs wounded by arrows, the Satvata, skilled in strength, shone in the battle, O king, like a flowering kimshuka tree."}},{"n":26,"text":"सात्यकिः समरे विद्धः केकयेन महात्मना ।\nकेकयं पञ्चविंशत्या विव्याध प्रहसन्निव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Pierced in battle by the great-souled Kekaya, Satyaki, as if laughing, pierced the Kekaya with twenty-five arrows."}},{"n":27,"text":"शतचन्द्रचिते गृह्य चर्मणी सुभुजौ तु तौ ।\nव्यरोचेतां महारङ्गे निस्त्रिंशवरधारिणौ ।\nयथा देवासुरे युद्धे जम्भशक्रौ महाबलौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"The two strong-armed men, taking shields marked with a hundred moons and fine swords, shone in the great arena, like mighty Jambha and Shakra in the battle of gods and asuras."}},{"n":28,"text":"मण्डलानि ततस्तौ च विचरन्तौ महारणे ।\nअन्योन्यमसिभिस्तूर्णं समाजघ्नतुराहवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, circling in the great battle, they quickly struck each other with their swords in the fight."}},{"n":29,"text":"केकयस्य ततश्चर्म द्विधा चिच्छेद सात्वतः ।\nसात्यकेश्च तथैवासौ चर्म चिच्छेद पार्थिवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Satvata cut the Kekaya's shield in two, and that king likewise cut Satyaki's shield."}},{"n":30,"text":"चर्म च्छित्त्वा तु कैकेयस्तारागणशतैर्वृतम् ।\nचचार मण्डलान्येव गतप्रत्यागतानि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having cut the shield, the Kekaya, which was adorned with hundreds of stars, kept moving in circles, advancing and retreating."}},{"n":31,"text":"तं चरन्तं महारङ्गे निस्त्रिंशवरधारिणम् ।\nअपहस्तेन चिच्छेद शैनेयस्त्वरयान्वितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As he moved in the great arena with his fine sword, Shini's grandson hurriedly cut him with a sword-throw."}},{"n":32,"text":"सवर्मा केकयो राजन्द्विधा छिन्नो महाहवे ।\nनिपपात महेष्वासो वज्रनुन्न इवाचलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Kekaya king with his armour, great archer, fell cut in two in the great fight, like a mountain struck by a thunderbolt."}},{"n":33,"text":"तं निहत्य रणे शूरः शैनेयो रथसत्तमः ।\nयुधामन्यो रथं तूर्णमारुरोह परंतपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having killed him in the battle, the hero Shaineya, best of chariot-fighters, scorcher of foes, quickly mounted Yudhamanyu's chariot."}},{"n":34,"text":"ततोऽन्यं रथमास्थाय विधिवत्कल्पितं पुनः ।\nकेकयानां महत्सैन्यं व्यधमत्सात्यकिः शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, mounting another chariot properly prepared, Satyaki again destroyed the great host of the Kekayas with arrows."}},{"n":35,"text":"सा वध्यमाना समरे केकयस्य महाचमूः ।\nतमुत्सृज्य रथं शत्रुं प्रदुद्राव दिशो दश ॥","meaning":{"en":"That great Kekaya force, being slaughtered in the battle, abandoned its chariot-fighter and fled in the ten directions."}}]}]}